# Build outputs and transient PyInstaller state — regenerated by
# build-release.ps1, never committed.
# Exception: payload/management/ (Parkos.psd1/.psm1/about_Parkos.help.txt) is
# first-party, versioned source, NOT a downloaded/build artifact - Get-ManagementModulePayload
# in build-release.ps1 validates it exists in the repo instead of fetching it.
# Exception: payload/README-EULA.txt is the End-User License Agreement - first-party
# legal document, not a build artifact. Show-Eula in parkos-installer.ps1 requires
# it to be present at install time (resolves via $script:PayloadRoot/README-EULA.txt).
payload/*
!payload/management/
!payload/README-EULA.txt
# Exception: payload/parts/ is the VERSIONED form of every large/third-party
# artifact: zip + parts <= 90 MiB (GitHub rejects single files > 100 MB) plus
# parts/payload-parts.json (see shared/ParkosPayloadParts.ps1, MANUAL.md). It
# includes the Postgres 16 binaries (parts/postgres). The RAW / unpacked forms
# stay ignored by payload/* above (services/, apps/, *.msi and nssm.exe at the
# payload root, pg_partman/, postgres/*.zip, .parts-sha256 markers): only the
# packed parts are versioned. payload/security/parkos-master.key is a company
# secret and must NEVER be committed (ignored by payload/*; never add it).
!payload/parts/
.pyinstaller-work/
__pycache__/
*.spec
